/* The camera permission prompt: shown when the reader first takes a photo, scans a document or reads a code, to attach to a message or to send when a bot asks for it. */
"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "Hermie uses the camera so you can take a photo, scan a document or read a code, to attach to a message or to send when a bot asks for it.";
/* The microphone permission prompt: shown when the reader first dictates a message or records a voice note. Dictation is recognised on the device and goes nowhere; a voice note is sent only on Send. */
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Hermie uses the microphone so you can dictate a message or record a voice note. Dictation is transcribed on this device and never sent anywhere; a voice note goes to your gateway only when you press Send.";
/* The speech recognition permission prompt: shown with the microphone's. Recognition runs on the device only, for dictation and for the transcript of a voice note. */
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "Hermie uses on-device speech recognition to turn what you say into the text of a message, or into a transcript of a voice note. Nothing is sent to Apple or to any other service.";
